# Line-ending policy. Without this file git has no rule, and on Windows a file
# written with CRLF sits permanently "modified" against an LF index — 3,610
# insertions and 3,610 deletions across four files, none of them real.
#
# That is not cosmetic. A `git status` that is never clean is a `git status`
# nobody reads, and this repository has already lost work to exactly that:
# tools/pronunciation_survey.py lived untracked for days, and the verdict
# ledger silently failed to commit, both visible in output that scrolled past.
#
# text=auto  - git normalises to LF in the object database
# eol=lf     - and checks out LF everywhere, so Windows, the Codemagic mac
#              runner and any cloud container all see identical bytes.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows shells need CRLF or they misbehave.
*.bat  text eol=crlf
*.cmd  text eol=crlf
*.ps1  text eol=crlf

# Never touch these. text=auto guesses well but guessing on a 38MB asset or a
# signing profile is not worth the one time it guesses wrong.
*.png       binary
*.jpg       binary
*.jpeg      binary
*.gif       binary
*.ico       binary
*.webp      binary
*.mp3       binary
*.wav       binary
*.ttf       binary
*.otf       binary
*.woff      binary
*.woff2     binary
*.jar       binary
*.keystore  binary
*.p12       binary
*.mobileprovision binary
